# --- Game files: never commit copyrighted assets -----------------------------
# GAME_PATH points at ./chaos by default; see docs/game-files.md.
# These are anchored to the repository root on purpose: an unanchored "game/"
# would also match the s6 service directory of the same name.
/chaos/
/game/
/chaos-overlords/

# Archives of the game, however they arrive. `git add -A` once swept a 7 MB
# chaos.zip and a stray file named after an IP address -- an scp missing its
# colon -- into a public commit. `/chaos/` matched neither, and the check that
# grepped for "^chaos/" and ".exe" did not either. Nothing here needs to track
# an archive, so refuse the whole class rather than those two names.
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.*
*.iso

# `scp file user@host` with the colon left out writes a local file named after
# the host. Those are always accidents.
[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*

# --- Python build artefacts ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Local configuration -----------------------------------------------------
/.env

# --- Scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.pcap
/*.png
/*.log
